SUMMARY:FASEB SRC: Dynamics and Encoding in Cell Signaling 2026 (2nd)
LOCATION:Millennium Hotel Maxwell House\, Nashville\, TN\, USA
DESCRIPTION:Second edition of the FASEB conference on how signalling inform
 ation is encoded\, transmitted and interpreted across space and time\, del
 iberately moving past static pathway diagrams toward a quantitative\, spat
 iotemporal account of signalling. Sessions covered receptor\, immune and m
 etabolic signalling\, developmental and spatial dynamics\, organoids and i
 ntravital imaging\, biosensors and optogenetic tool development\, signalli
 ng dynamics in cancer\, and cell death\, senescence and the cell cycle\, w
 ith an emphasis on the imaging and modelling methods behind them.\n\nWhy i
 t matters for mTOR (★): mTOR is named nowhere in the programme\; the rel
 evance runs through one keynote speaker and through the method. Jin Zhang 
 (UC San Diego) is a keynote\, and he is the author of the Atlas study that
  first put a FRET biosensor on mTORC1 activity in single living cells – 
 dynamic\, time-resolved regulation of mTOR being my current research focus
 . The sessions on biosensors and optogenetic tool development and on metab
 olic signalling are the part of this meeting that bears on that question: 
 this is where the instruments for watching the pathway in real time get bu
 ilt\, even though the pathway itself is not on the poster.\n\nSpeakers or 
 organisers with a profile in the Atlas: Jin Zhang\n\nConference site: http
 s://events.faseb.org/Dynamics-Encoding-Cell-Signaling\n\nIn Oliver's mTOR 
 Atlas: https://mtor-atlas.org/events/#ev-faseb-src-dynamics-and-encoding-i
 n-cell-signaling-2026-2nd
